a y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"tsaifr1x7MHWsUngvZ1SQA","review_id":"JbGZ0CTsPoeoZ3YgGT-blw","date":"2017-05-25T12:42:25","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9534398913383484,"text_excerpt":"I can't believe I haven't reviewed this place before now. Anyway, I've been coming to this location for years and have never had a bad experience. Is it loud sometimes? Yes. Is it insanely crowded sometimes? Hell yeah. But it's really good sushi and drinks. Recently, I have started taking advantage of their Thank God It's Tuesday specials of $5 cocktails and $5 LSU rolls, which is a really good deal (I think the LSU roll is usually $14). Additionally, it can be crowded on a Tuesday, but it's not nearly as busy at it can be on a Friday or Saturday night which is cool. My husband isn't too into sushi so he orders the Airline Chicken breast and, Lord, it's so good! So, if you're not the raw ..."},{"business_id":"tsaifr1x7MHWsUngvZ1SQA","review_id":"i1sNjXYCZXiTlliNUZofLA","date":"2010-12-17T07:44:21","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9487887620925903,"text_excerpt":"My favorite sushi place in the city. I like the decor and atmosphere of the place. Sushi's always fresh and it's one of the few Asian places where you'll see non-Asians on their waitstaff. It also completely fits in the Warehouse District and is a good place to stop before the Red Eye. I used to many nights- before, during and after college. Been there many times with friends and they've never disappointed. Service is always fast and knowledgeable. You never have to wait long for the food. They've got classic New Orleans rolls and use fresh ingredients in them. The rolls are on the smaller side but since they stay open later than everyone else, you don't really fault them for it. Also a v..."},{"business_id":"tsaifr1x7MHWsUngvZ1SQA","review_id":"-ey5xyoQy-p98VI8GO77QQ","date":"2011-01-22T19:54:29","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9480039477348328,"text_excerpt":"One of the best things about this place -- it's within walking distance for me! Score! But seriously, I can eat sushi any and everyday, several times a day, so that really is a big deal! The vibe of this place is fun -- top 40 music over the speakers -- kind of close to eating sushi in a well lit club. I've read some reviews that have been critical of the loud, drunk, obnoxious people, so you have to understand the atmosphere you're getting yourself into. I, personally, think it's fun and good for people watching! As for the sushi, it's good, but not blow your mind good. Coming from LA, there's a gazillion good sushi places with super fresh fish, and Rock-n-Sake gets the job done, but kin..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"tsaifr1x7MHWsUngvZ1SQA","photo_id":"-_cmODMy6brwQtyyLGYylg","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/-_cmODMy6brwQtyyLGYylg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.878